WEBVTT - Cosmic Dawn

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.500
For 25 years, NASA has been filming the journey of the

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.500
James Webb Space Telescope.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.600
This is a never before seen look.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.000
I'm excited for people to see the drama—

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.980
Holy [rocket roaring]

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.800
...of what it takes to make a space telescope.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.500
Nature has this way of being even more creative than we are.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.720
We have always been surprised by what we see in the sky.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.620
That's why building a telescope has always been interesting.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.300
The voyage back to the birth of the universe.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.520
These decades of work of thousands of people around the

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.960
world to make this telescope possible.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.000
Okay, gonna have lots of inventions along the way.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.780
Now how can we justify this to our constituents?

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.160
We're gonna change how we understand the universe.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.040
Science is a process.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.780
All six metric tons of this has to be launched a

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:06.480
million miles out into outer space.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.920
Isn't that kinda crazy not to be able to service it?

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.060
And lift off.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.800
Yeah, that's the only choice we had.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.300
I really wanted to honor what an incredible mission this was.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.700
We were on edge, from blizzards to hurricanes.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.220
There was nothing easy about Webb at all.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.500
On to the pressure.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:31.000
There was something different about this one.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.060
You knew you were in the middle of something big.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.560
We're gonna see all the way back to the very beginning of the universe,

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.500
what we call Cosmic Dawn.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:51.000
[Dramatic music crescendo]
